# Benchmarks

Correctness first, then **measure on the same PR**. Phase 2 is for speeding up. Do not wait until Phase 2 to time or count allocations.

- Time: [criterion](https://docs.rs/criterion). Entry `benches/exact.rs`. Command `just bench` (enables the non-default `bench-internals` feature for `gprx::internals`).
- Allocations: `tests/alloc.rs` runs in `just test`. Count after Workspace setup. Ratchet: the allowed count must stay or fall, never rise without an Issue.
- Fixed problems (`n = 256` required from P1A-18; `512` / `1024` when they finish in seconds). Isotropic groups: 1-D Forrester `f(x)=(6x-2)²sin(12x-4)` on `[0, 1]`, RBF + `GaussianLikelihood` + `StandardizeTarget`, start `ℓ = 1`. ARD groups: 2-D weighted sphere `f=(x/0.25)²+(y/1)²` on a 16×16 grid (`mll_and_grad_ard` / `fit_lbfgs_ard`), start `ℓ_d = 4` (`ℓ_d = 1` dies in the first line search). `y` is the named function plus `N(0, 1)` from the crate `SeededRng` (Forrester seed `0`; ARD sphere seed `9` — seed `0` walks a ridge on Never), not an independent random series. `σn²` starts at `0.1`. Compare ARD Always vs Never; do not compare those groups to isotropic `phase-1b`. Historical `phase-1a` / `phase-1b` numbers used `d = 8` and random `y` — do not mix those times with this problem.
- Split benches. Never mix "one MLL+grad" with "full L-BFGS fit". When logging `fit_lbfgs` / `fit_lbfgs_ard`, record the joint-eval count. Do not treat a wall-time delta as a speedup if the eval counts differ.
- `just bench` is local. Default CI does not run criterion (noisy). Alloc tests stay in `just test`.
- PR that touches a hot path (`kernel/`, `workspace`, `gpr`, `objective`, `online`): paste criterion vs previous named baseline in Verification, or write why it cannot change speed.
- Do not add SIMD, Rayon, mixed precision, or cache "for speed" unless a bench on this problem shows that path is the bottleneck. Isotropic RBF / distance SIMD is already in (`src/kernel/simd.rs`). ARD `(Δx_d)²` fill and RBF ARD `apply`/`grad` SIMD are in with the P2-7 cache. Isotropic Periodic / RQ square Gram and weighted gradient SIMD are in (`src/kernel/stationary_simd.rs`, #374), and so is `f32` isotropic RBF on widened `f64` lanes (#385). Judge more SIMD on `kernel_rbf` / `predict` / `FIXED` / ARD kernel paths, not only on `mll_and_grad`.
- Named baselines: `phase-1a`, `phase-1b`, `phase-2`. Save with criterion; log the machine and the numbers in `.dev/bench-log.md` (local, not committed). After P2-9, compare new work to `phase-2` (isotropic vs `phase-1b` on the Forrester remasure; ARD Always vs Never). Do not mix those times with the historical `d = 8` random-`y` rows. Do not start Phase 3 without that log.
- Strategy detail: `docs/design.md` §15.
